{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1008368-advices-for-bigger-challenges-rank-4-upwards","id":1008368,"title":"advices for bigger challenges? (rank 4 upwards?)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-25T18:58:57-08:00","id":1008368,"title":"advices for bigger challenges? (rank 4 upwards?)","content":"i was thinking a lot about this. i got an Ahroun get of fenris (young mother now) who just jumped to rank 4 and a corax as well.. the GoF is stacking a lot of gifts to increase her strenght and willpower as wel to soak A LOT. i feel like my BDS are not pulling enough punches...any advices to give a proper challenge? something to hold her against the ropes? as well any ideas or suggestions for a test for her to jump to the next rank? im thinking about soemthing that could sacrifice her actual relationship with her mate and her family (which is incredibly important to her)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T21:11:16-08:00","id":1008405,"title":"","content":"High ranking Get Ahroun are pretty hard to kill. Unless she is constantly fighting other high ranking BSDs (unlikely), she will probably be facing inferior foes. Design some big nasty spirits for her to fight, fallen incarna avatars if need be.<br /> <br /> I would *not* ask her to sacrifice things that she cares about as part of a rank challenge. Maybe threaten them with your villains, but saying 'choose between your rank or your family' seems like an idiotic thing for a Master of a Challenge to come up with. Why would the elders or spirits want to sabotage the already rocky home lives of the Garou?<br /> <br /> From an out of game perspective, if your players have an innocent aspect of the game they enjoy, I would think long and hard before snatching that thing away. It may encourage them not to get attached to anything.<br /> <br /> I am gonna quote Torakhan who had a good summary in an earlier thread this year:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/850823-challenge-for-rank?p=851598#post851598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Rank Challenges to become Athro are damned hard. They can take months to accomplish, often trying to do great and heroic things to show that you can step up beyond the every-man that is expected and become greater. You may spend a great deal of time going through Umbral Realms, recovering lost relics. A whole pack becoming Athro at once is unlikely, but... not outside of the realm of possibility--but it's likely not the same group that started as Claiths (most Garou don't make it to this Rank, let alone deserve it.)</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I would focus on the difficulty and heroism of the challenge, rather than focusing on cheap emotional shots. Maybe a quest to Malfeas or the Atrocity realm in search of someone or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 11-26-2016, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T03:53:24-08:00","id":1008476,"title":"","content":"Honestly, at Athro, the question should no longer be can you fight tougher and tougher foes for an Ahroun. You can.<br /> <br /> Now, you need to -lead- and ensure others survive those fights. You need to prove that you can lead a war party and keep everyone alive. You need to prove you are more than a tool by showing eye for strategy and planning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T05:31:12-08:00","id":1008500,"title":"","content":"I second Ana on that. While every Ahroun has their archetype, there is only so far a bad ass should be able to get in the Nation on those individual strengths without being able fulfill the rest of their Auspice role, or live up the &quot;teacher&quot; part of being an Athro. As an Athro Ahroun, you have to <i>double</i> your Wisdom, and almost double your Honor to reach Elder, going by numbers alone. You need only one more point of Glory. I think that's indicative of what the Nation expects of Ahroun who survive that long, of them needing to really rise and become more. It's a hint for what to throw at them, while still being relevant to their Auspice role.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what the structure of your game is or anything about character beyond what you've said, but assuming there is a Pack and maybe a Sept involved, you can challenge bad asses like this not with 1v1, but by challenging her group. If she's crushing foes that face her, give her too many to face - not to steamroll her, but to force her to delegate, to command, to lead, to coordinate. Arrange an organic reason that makes sense as to why she might not be able to get involved directly, herself, and perhaps has to lead from afar through whatever means her Pack might have (pack link, etc). Give her a monster that simply can't be slain through straight damage but has to actually be figured out to be defeated, such as having the equivalent of a phylactery, or the like. Make her choose between attaining the glory of a killing blow, or putting her impressive soak and skin under fire to hold the line while her allies have to be the ones to do damage because none of them are thick-skinned enough to weather the onslaught.<br /> <br /> Also, if you're finding the power creep to be an issue, then make things more difficult to purchase. (Again, I don't anything about the game or how it's run, so these are just general suggestions.) Don't just let people buy up Willpower (or whatever), make sure there is good justification for how and why. Have they <i>really</i> been working on it? Make the scenes where they are learning Gifts from the spirits longer, more demanding, requiring more sacrifice of some kind. But ultimately, you also just need to be flexible and know the characters well enough to understand what challenges them on a more personal basis, without using it punitively - or be comfortable opening up the scope of the game to higher stakes, more legendary tasks, and more outlandish places, like Laughing Stranger suggested. (Also, Atrocity would be a great place to send a really hard-to-kill Fenrir, especially if the character or player doesn't know or won't metagame that you have to die to get out, in most cases, IIRC.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T13:27:52-08:00","id":1008661,"title":"","content":"Don't go with a Black Spiral Dancer. Use some other difficult monster instead - maybe a Thunderwyrm or a monster of your own devising inspired by horror stories or movies - if you are looking for a physical challenge. Figure out what stats you want to have first, and then create the monster around it.<br /> <br /> If the increase is rank is due to wisdom or honor, and you want the challenge to incorporate that, then include those elements as part of the quest to be done before they fight the monster. Maybe they have to figure out what the monster is first, or where it is located, or the special macguffin they need to kill it.<br /> <br /> I like Laughing Stranger's quote from Torakhan that Athro challenges can take many months of in game time to achieve. At that level, it really becomes a core part of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T06:20:57-08:00","id":1010172,"title":"","content":"Question cause I'm new to playing werewolf. Is it common for pack members to reach ranks at different points? How do STs deal with envy and inequality? I would hate to be the only pack member stuck at Rank 1 while another has been Rank 2 for awhile and maybe another is getting close to Rank 3. In the current game I'm playing (the first werewolf game I've played) the group is pretty much on pace to all rank up at the same time which I like (though I should also ask if it's normal for the pack to gain renown as a pack or is it normally individualized based on character actions?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T06:45:29-08:00","id":1010181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrostFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1008368-advices-for-bigger-challenges-rank-4-upwards?p=1010172#post1010172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question cause I'm new to playing werewolf. Is it common for pack members to reach ranks at different points? How do STs deal with envy and inequality? I would hate to be the only pack member stuck at Rank 1 while another has been Rank 2 for awhile and maybe another is getting close to Rank 3. In the current game I'm playing (the first werewolf game I've played) the group is pretty much on pace to all rank up at the same time which I like (though I should also ask if it's normal for the pack to gain renown as a pack or is it normally individualized based on character actions?).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've certainly played in games run both ways. But it isn't abnormal for pack members to have a rank difference for a while. As long as it's a difference by only 1 Rank I've found it doesn't matter much. If and when the Rank difference gets to 2 ranks, then it's time to do something as a ST imo. <br /> First game I played in though, we didn't keep track of Renown so specifically and the whole pack went through Rank challenges together every so often. The game was fun and that's what matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T20:15:49-08:00","id":1010469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrostFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1008368-advices-for-bigger-challenges-rank-4-upwards?p=1010172#post1010172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question cause I'm new to playing werewolf. Is it common for pack members to reach ranks at different points? How do STs deal with envy and inequality? I would hate to be the only pack member stuck at Rank 1 while another has been Rank 2 for awhile and maybe another is getting close to Rank 3. In the current game I'm playing (the first werewolf game I've played) the group is pretty much on pace to all rank up at the same time which I like (though I should also ask if it's normal for the pack to gain renown as a pack or is it normally individualized based on character actions?).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Generally I handle the renown as the Soryteller and try to have the pack gain rank together. I also try to keep everyone's rank challenge to fit the Auspice. In the past I had widely varying ranks in Packs as Players died and new ones took their place. I used a few different means to equal things out and finally developed my own system for integrating new characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T21:45:35-08:00","id":1010505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1008368-advices-for-bigger-challenges-rank-4-upwards?p=1010469#post1010469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and finally developed my own system for integrating new characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do tell, if you don't mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T22:07:32-08:00","id":1010513,"title":"","content":"The System is as follows: I allow the player to start at the rank of the pack, and the person is given rank x 15 freebie points. They must buy all gifts from this pool minus the 3 starting gifts the player also keeps any and all experience points that they had at the time of death, but they must all be used on the new character at creation. The player by vote of the other players/my fiat maybe given a set number of extra &quot;free gifts&quot; this only comes into play in and yes these are real examples:<br /> 1. The Pack Theurge Rank 2 on the cusp of Rank 3(and yes would have made it following this fight) is knocked down the flight of stairs into the basement and into the Maul of a Bane. The Bane savages the character, she has 1 health level left. Rather than run or try to escape or even dodge the player instead spends Gnosis and heals the Ahroun spending willpower to ensure success and lets the pack win even as she dies. By vote of the other players the new character was made rank 3 to fit with the rest except for the Ragabash that choose to run from the fight and was the person that knocked the theurge down the stairs in the first place. This player got 3 level two gifts for free as well as the starting gifts.<br /> 2. The Ragabash in the above example later decides to go exploring taking another member with them in a small Wyrm tainted town mostly because he was miffed that the rest of the pack was scouting out a neighboring town to see if the Taint was localized or wide spread. The Ragabash and the other player were caught and died in a suitably gruesome manner. The Pack did attempt a rescue, but there were 2 botches during the attempt and the stealth rescue became an all out war. Note this group was oversized and I had 8 players. I gave this player no free gifts, but did make him the same rank as the rest of the pack.<br /> Final portion of this rule if over 50% of the pack dies in any given situation I require a new totem be sought and if 100% of a Pack dies I take a vote on whether to continue the story or abort.<br /> If continuing the story, the new pack is sent to investigate what happened to the old and generally are 1 rank lower. My players tend to die through either bad luck example 1 or stupidity example 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T02:48:20-08:00","id":1010561,"title":"","content":"I think that Ana Mizuki and The laughing Stranger hit it on the nail. The higher rank challenges go beyond do this, find this, kill this. To become true elders and leaders of the Garou they need to prove they can think out of the box and go beyond their safety zone. Sure, the Get may be a glorious fighter, so how does she handle teaching this to others? Or working with others beyond her pack? Test her and challenge her by going to the wider definition of the Ahroun.<br /> <br /> And do not make the family a sacrifice for the Challenge. It's just dickery. Especially when you have a fighting machine that actually has real links and ties to the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}